.SH "NAME"
systemd-factory-reset-generator \- Pull factory\-reset\-now\&.target into the initial boot transaction when factory reset has been requested
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
/usr/lib/systemd/system\-generators/systemd\-factory\-reset\-generator
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
systemd\-factory\-reset\-generator
is a generator that pulls
factory\-reset\-now\&.target
into the initial boot transaction when the factory reset operation has been requested, either via the
\fIsystemd\&.factory_reset=\fR
kernel command line option or via the
\fIFactoryResetRequest\fR
EFI variable\&.
.PP
systemd\-factory\-reset\-generator
implements
\fBsystemd.generator\fR(7)\&.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
\fBsystemd\fR(1), \fBsystemd-factory-reset\fR(8), \m[blue]\fBFactory Reset\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[1]\d\s+2
.SH "NOTES"
.IP " 1." 4
Factory Reset
